From 424ff267161189bac9ef6fca3e26dd7e16737169 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ericek111 <erik.brocko@letemsvetemapplem.eu>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:21:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 33/50] highmem: kunmap writes a non-write-back page's lines
 out of the CPU cache

The kernel view of a page stays write-back on macOS. TTM clears pooled write-combined pages through it,
and the dirty lines were later written back over the GPU's non-snooped writes: a 64 MB fill into
HOST_COHERENT (write-combined) memory read back up to 10% zeros.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DP5dwQG4pUvK6V9ftNsQRB
---
 override/include/linux/highmem.h | 214 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 214 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 override/include/linux/highmem.h

